{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund NHS BSL interpreters and deaf awareness training",
        "additional_details": "Patients may not hear their names being called in A&E, clinics or appointments and can face delays in accessing qualified BSL interpreters. We are concerned that this can affect communication, informed consent, patient safety and dignity, particularly before operations and during emergencies. NHS hospitals should provide timely BSL interpreters and deaf awareness training for staff.",
        "background": "Deaf BSL users can face barriers in A&E and NHS appointments. Some patients can't hear their names being called or access a BSL interpreter when needed. The government should ensure all hospitals provide timely BSL interpreters and deaf awareness training for staff.",
